  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Peel the carrot, then shred using a julienne peeler or coarsely grate with a box grater. Separate the pak choy leaves. Put the char siu sauce and 1 tbs white vinegar in a bowl, season with pepper and stir to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/675924/photos/large/127516_1-0df1d2f0b0430756d97754714d3401df.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make stock: Crumble 1 stock cube into a heatproof jug, add 500ml (2 cups) boiling water and 1 tbs soy sauce and stir to dissolve.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/675925/photos/large/127516_2-b711788234fc227b14ff3768b296cb13.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Start soup: Heat a drizzle of vegetable oil in a medium saucepan over medium-high heat. Cook the carrot, stirring, for 2 mins or until slightly softened. Add the stock and bring to the boil.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/675926/photos/large/127516_3-f54bf79f106e04473b66785ae8597a99.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook dumplings: Add the dumplings to the stock mixture and cook for 2 mins. Add the pak choy and cook for a further 2 mins or until the dumplings are tender and the pak choy is wilted. Remove the pan from the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/675927/photos/large/127516_4-7e01b8bb446e283b437cf2ab55a85bfc.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Divide the dumpling soup among bowls (see Kitchen 101). Drizzle with the char siu mixture, scatter with the sesame seeds and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/675928/photos/large/127516_5-355d9c52f12e044080d5361d1cea9936.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen 101: Handle the cooked dumplings with love and care to ensure they don't break up or burst open.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/675929/photos/large/127516_6-3d6466c94b15d7bb4835cb1f57009ec7.jpeg"
    }
  ]
